{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773178658,"nonce":"EaRl/F/zkgXDCvDf+9eFIAEN5zw=","title":"spec_to_graph ignores Network subgraph — always builds SimpleStagedNetwork black box","message":"In serialization.py, spec_to_graph checks for node_spec.type == \"Network\" and immediately calls _build_network(), which constructs a SimpleStagedNetwork from outer params only. Any user-defined subgraph for the Network node is completely ignored. This is the deepest graph-as-model violation remaining: the canvas graph is not used to build the model for Network nodes. Fix requires implementing a subgraph-aware Network builder that reads hidden_type/hidden_size from the subgraph cell node and readout activation from the Linear node (partially done in _extract_graph_params) but builds the actual model from the subgraph topology.","files":null}]}